Double Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "353966"} "Coxless Pairs, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "353979"} "Quadruple Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "353991"} "Coxless Fours, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354004"} "Eights, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354013"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "354046"} "Single Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "354078"} "Double Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "354091"} "Coxless Pairs, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "354105"} "Quadruple Sculls, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "354114"} "Eights, Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "354122"} "Lightweight Double Sculls, Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "159456"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "159637"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "159816"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "261063"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "319040"} "2012"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/391"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Lightweight Coxless Fours, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "6 – 11 August 2016"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/912"} "Estádio da Lagoa, Lagoa Rodrigo de Freitas, Rio de Janeiro"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/354033"} "52 from 13 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "South Africa had been the surprise winners of the Men’s Lightweight Coxless Fours at the 2012 Summer Olympics, but they were not present in the event in Rio to defend their title. Denmark had long been the strongest nation in this event and, since their bronze medal finish at the 2012 Games, " [:a {:href "/athletes/122915"} "Kasper Winther Jørgensen"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/118064"} "Morten Jørgensen"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/123147"} "Jacob Barsøe"] " had been the 2013 and 2014 World and European Champions, the 2015 World runners-up, and the 2015 European bronze medalists. In Rio they were joined by long-time partner " [:a {:href "/athletes/133506"} "Jacob Larsen"] ", but faced a serious challenge from the Swiss quartet of " [:a {:href "/athletes/126361"} "Lucas Tramèr"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/126359"} "Simon Schürch"] ", " [:a {:href "/athletes/126358"} "Simon Niepmann"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/126356"} "Mario Gyr"] ", who were the 2015 World and 2015 and 2016 European Champions."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Denmark won its heat by over three seconds during the preliminaries, with Switzerland close behind Italy and China in its heat, but still far ahead of fourth-place finisher France. New Zealand, the 2013 and 2014 World runners-up, captured the third heat, before coming in third behind Italy and France in the first semifinal. Switzerland and Denmark, meanwhile, were well ahead of the competition in the second semifinal and would go on to win gold and silver respectively in the final. Third place went to France, the 2015 World bronze medalists and European runners-up, coming in nearly three seconds ahead of Italy."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "Switzerland"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/126361"} "Lucas Tramèr"] " • " [: